                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Atomic swap: Nonminimal contract push"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Atomic swap: Unconfirmed bitcoin commitment. Categories: Atomic swap. Weaknesses: CWE-841."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Atomic swap: Unconfirmed bitcoin commitment. Categories: Atomic swap. Weaknesses: CWE-841.\n\n## Remediation\n\nWhen Bitcoin is the initiating leg, require current, fully funded, sufficiently confirmed and unspent Bitcoin funding in the core before creating the Zenon HTLC. Recheck before submitting a prepared create, and make Auto Mode wait until the condition holds.",
                "text": "Atomic swap: Unconfirmed bitcoin commitment. Categories: Atomic swap. Weaknesses: CWE-841.\n\nRemediation:\n\nWhen Bitcoin is the initiating leg, require current, fully funded, sufficiently confirmed and unspent Bitcoin funding in the core before creating the Zenon HTLC. Recheck before submitting a prepared create, and make Auto Mode wait until the condition holds."
              },
              "id": "atomic-swap.unconfirmed-bitcoin-commitment",
              "name": "Atomic swap: Unconfirmed bitcoin commitment",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "8.0",
                "tags": [
                  "atomic-swap",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-841",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Atomic swap: Unconfirmed bitcoin commitment"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Command injection: Offer amount cli. Categories: Command injection. Weaknesses: CWE-78."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Command injection: Offer amount cli. Categories: Command injection. Weaknesses: CWE-78.\n\n## Remediation\n\nValidate positive bounded decimal amounts at offer decoding and core swap creation. POSIX-shell-quote every interpolated argument in CLI output, including amounts, HTLC identifiers and node URLs, and avoid emitting runnable commands while mandatory fields remain invalid.",
                "text": "Command injection: Offer amount cli. Categories: Command injection. Weaknesses: CWE-78.\n\nRemediation:\n\nValidate positive bounded decimal amounts at offer decoding and core swap creation. POSIX-shell-quote every interpolated argument in CLI output, including amounts, HTLC identifiers and node URLs, and avoid emitting runnable commands while mandatory fields remain invalid."
              },
              "id": "command-injection.offer-amount-cli",
              "name": "Command injection: Offer amount cli",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "5.0",
                "tags": [
                  "command-injection",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-078",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Command injection: Offer amount cli"
              }
            },
            {
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of service: Board inbox timestamp. Categories: Denial of service. Weaknesses: CWE-20, CWE-248."
              },
              "help": {
                "markdown": "Denial of service: Board inbox timestamp. Categories: Denial of service. Weaknesses: CWE-20, CWE-248.\n\n## Remediation\n\nReject unsupported or implausible event timestamps in the take read boundary before adding requests to inbox state, and use a total date-formatting helper that returns a fallback for invalid dates. Add source-level regression coverage for a validly signed/encrypted take with an out-of-range created_at and for mixed valid/invalid inbox requests so malformed data cannot disable dismiss controls.",
                "text": "Denial of service: Board inbox timestamp. Categories: Denial of service. Weaknesses: CWE-20, CWE-248.\n\nRemediation:\n\nReject unsupported or implausible event timestamps in the take read boundary before adding requests to inbox state, and use a total date-formatting helper that returns a fallback for invalid dates. Add source-level regression coverage for a validly signed/encrypted take with an out-of-range created_at and for mixed valid/invalid inbox requests so malformed data cannot disable dismiss controls."
              },
              "id": "denial-of-service.board-inbox-timestamp",
              "name": "Denial of service: Board inbox timestamp",
              "properties": {
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "denial-of-service",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-020",
                  "external/cwe/cwe-248",
                  "security"
                ]
              },
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Denial of service: Board inbox timestamp"
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.1.24"
        }
      }
